        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party operator` BECAUSE "the failure to comply with a commitment is subject to administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(4)"

-- src:1236 | The supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to the AI Office in reply to a request shall be subject to administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(5).
@ref Art 75c(4) third subparagraph (src:1236)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information supplied to the AI Office in reply to a request is incorrect, incomplete or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75c(4) third subparagraph the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to the AI Office in reply to a request is subject to administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(5)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the information supplied to the AI Office in reply to a request is incorrect, incomplete or misleading`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- the supply is within the sentence
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to the AI Office in reply to a request" (split site (i), fork F-75c-4-supply)

-- src:1236 | The supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to the AI Office in reply to a request shall be subject to administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(5).
@ref Art 75c(4) third subparagraph (src:1236)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has made a request for information to the operator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75c act`
`Art 75c(4) the operator's bar on supplying incorrect, incomplete or misleading information` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the AI Office has made a request for information to the operator`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is barred: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the facts the bar is about do not all hold
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party operator`
        SHANT `Art 75c(4) supply incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to the AI Office in reply to a request`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party operator` BECAUSE "the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to the AI Office in reply to a request is subject to administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(5)"

§ `Article 75c(5): periodic penalty payments`

-- src:1237 | 5. The AI Office may adopt a decision imposing periodic penalty payments to compel the operators subject to its competence pursuant to Article 75(1) to the following:
-- src:1238 | (a) to submit to an investigation;
-- src:1239 | (b) to comply with an information request ordered by a decision adopted under Article 75a(3);
-- src:1240 | (c) to submit to an inspection ordered by a decision pursuant to Article 75a(4);
-- src:1241 | (d) to provide correct or complete answers or explanations in the context of an inspection ordered by a decision pursuant to Article 75a(4);
-- src:1242 | (e) to comply with corrective actions ordered pursuant to the power listed in Article 16 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020;
-- src:1243 | (f) to comply with commitments made legally binding by a decision pursuant to Article 75b; or
-- src:1244 | (g) to comply with a decision pursuant to the paragraph (1) of this Article.
@ref Art 75c(5) first subparagraph and points (a) to (g) (src:1237-1244)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the operator is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose` IS A `Art 75c(5) purpose of the periodic penalty payments`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75c(5) the AI Office may adopt a decision imposing periodic penalty payments to compel the operator to` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `the purpose`
         WHEN `Art 75c(5) any other purpose that the list does not name` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "to the following:" is followed by a list that no "only" closes
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the operator is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "the operators subject to its competence pursuant to Article 75(1)", with no "only" (ruling (c))

-- src:1237 | 5. The AI Office may adopt a decision imposing periodic penalty payments to compel the operators subject to its competence pursuant to Article 75(1) to the following:
@ref Art 75c(5) first subparagraph (src:1237)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the operator is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75c act`
`Art 75c(5) the AI Office's choice to adopt a decision imposing periodic penalty payments` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the operator is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MAY `Art 75c(5) adopt a decision imposing periodic penalty payments`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- The limit: "shall not exceed 5 % of the average daily income or worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year per day". The base is one figure that the asker supplies (fork F-75c-5-base).
-- src:1245 | Those penalty payments shall be effective and proportionate, and, where applicable, shall not exceed 5 % of the average daily income or worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year per day, calculated from the date appointed by the decision.
@ref Art 75c(5) second subparagraph (src:1245)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the limit applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the average daily income or the worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 75c(5) second subparagraph the limit on the periodic penalty payment per day` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the limit applies`
         THEN JUST ((`the average daily income or the worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year` TIMES 5) DIVIDED BY 100)  -- "shall not exceed 5 % of the average daily income or worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year per day"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where applicable" limits the cap; the text does not say when it is not applicable

-- src:1245 | Those penalty payments shall be effective and proportionate, and, where applicable, shall not exceed 5 % of the average daily income or worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year per day, calculated from the date appointed by the decision.
@ref Art 75c(5) second subparagraph (src:1245)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the limit applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the average daily income or the worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the periodic penalty payment per day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75c(5) second subparagraph the periodic penalty payment per day is barred as exceeding the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 75c(5) second subparagraph the limit on the periodic penalty payment per day` `the date asked` `the limit applies` `the average daily income or the worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no limit arises on these facts (see the function above)
    WHEN JUST `the limit` THEN
        IF `the periodic penalty payment per day` GREATER THAN `the limit`
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those penalty payments shall ... not exceed 5 %" (a flat negative: the bar holds)
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a payment within the limit is not made lawful by this sentence, which also asks that payments be "effective and proportionate"

-- src:1245 | Those penalty payments shall be effective and proportionate, and, where applicable, shall not exceed 5 % of the average daily income or worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year per day, calculated from the date appointed by the decision.
@ref Art 75c(5) second subparagraph (src:1245)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the limit applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the average daily income or the worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the periodic penalty payment per day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75c act`
`Art 75c(5) second subparagraph the AI Office's bar on imposing a periodic penalty payment above the limit` MEANS
    IF `Art 75c(5) second subparagraph the periodic penalty payment per day is barred as exceeding the limit` `the date asked` `the limit applies` `the average daily income or the worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year` `the periodic penalty payment per day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        SHANT `Art 75c(5) impose a periodic penalty payment per day above the limit`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office` BECAUSE "a periodic penalty payment above 5 % per day was imposed"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is barred on these facts

-- src:1245 | Those penalty payments shall be effective and proportionate, and, where applicable, shall not exceed 5 % of the average daily income or worldwide annual turnover in the preceding financial year per day, calculated from the date appointed by the decision.
@ref Art 75c(5) second subparagraph last words (src:1245)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date appointed by the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 75c(5) second subparagraph the periodic penalty payment is calculated from the date appointed by the decision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST `the date appointed by the decision`  -- "calculated from the date appointed by the decision"

