§ `Article 75c(8): limitation periods`

-- src:1248 | 8. The powers conferred on the AI Office by this Article shall be subject to a limitation period of five years. The limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement is committed. However, in the case of continuing or repeated infringements, the limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement ceases.
@ref Art 75c(8) first subparagraph (src:1248)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the infringement is committed` IS A DATE
      `the infringement is continuing or repeated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the infringement ceases` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 75c(8) first subparagraph the day on which the limitation period of the powers of the AI Office begins to run` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the infringement is continuing or repeated`
         THEN JUST `the date the infringement ceases`  -- "in the case of continuing or repeated infringements, the limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement ceases"
         ELSE JUST `the date the infringement is committed`  -- "The limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement is committed"

-- The period "of five years" that begins on a day is taken to end on the fifth anniversary of that day, which is its last day (assumed, not ruled; fork F-75c-8-last-day).
-- src:1248 | 8. The powers conferred on the AI Office by this Article shall be subject to a limitation period of five years. The limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement is committed. However, in the case of continuing or repeated infringements, the limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement ceases.
@ref Art 75c(8) first subparagraph (src:1248)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the infringement is committed` IS A DATE
      `the infringement is continuing or repeated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the infringement ceases` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 75c(8) first subparagraph the last day of the limitation period of the powers of the AI Office` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 75c(8) first subparagraph the day on which the limitation period of the powers of the AI Office begins to run` `the date asked` `the date the infringement is committed` `the infringement is continuing or repeated` `the date the infringement ceases`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no start day arises on these facts (see the function above)
    WHEN JUST `the first day` THEN JUST (`add months` `the first day` 60)  -- "a limitation period of five years"

-- src:1248 | 8. The powers conferred on the AI Office by this Article shall be subject to a limitation period of five years. The limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement is committed. However, in the case of continuing or repeated infringements, the limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement ceases.
@ref Art 75c(8) first subparagraph (src:1248)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the infringement is committed` IS A DATE
      `the infringement is continuing or repeated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the infringement ceases` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75c(8) first subparagraph the powers of the AI Office are barred by the limitation period on the date asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 75c(8) first subparagraph the last day of the limitation period of the powers of the AI Office` `the date asked` `the date the infringement is committed` `the infringement is continuing or repeated` `the date the infringement ceases`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no limitation period arises on these facts (see the function above)
    WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN
        IF `the date asked` AT MOST `the last day`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling (a) of 2026-11-05: inside the five years the powers are not barred, and a date before the period begins (the day of the infringement, or the day it ceases) is outside it too, so it answers the same (fork F-75c-8-inside)
        ELSE JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The powers conferred on the AI Office by this Article shall be subject to a limitation period of five years" (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling (a): once it has run, the powers are barred)

-- src:1248 | 8. The powers conferred on the AI Office by this Article shall be subject to a limitation period of five years. The limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement is committed. However, in the case of continuing or repeated infringements, the limitation period shall begin to run on the day on which the infringement ceases.
@ref Art 75c(8) first subparagraph (src:1248)
